WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.090
A restaurant analytics system connects browser activity, server events, and dashboard reporting.

2
00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:22.180
The application uses React, Express, SQLite, and reusable tracking clients.

3
00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:31.533
Opening the menu generates a page-view event through the browser SDK.

4
00:00:31.533 --> 00:00:40.887
An anonymous visitor ID links activity; session IDs rotate after thirty minutes of inactivity.

5
00:00:40.887 --> 00:00:50.240
Page tracking excludes URL query parameters and fragments.

6
00:00:50.240 --> 00:01:01.140
Filtering categories and adding items generate custom browser events.

7
00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:12.040
The pizza and citrus cooler total ₹640. Events are queued and delivered in batches.

8
00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:22.940
Transient delivery failures retry with the same event IDs, preventing duplicate persistence.

9
00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:27.440
The server calculates the ₹640 order price from its own menu.

10
00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:31.940
Order and server event persist in one transaction; retrying the same order key does not create a duplicate.

11
00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:36.440
Dashboard metrics are calculated from stored events, rather than browser-local counters.

12
00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:40.940
The report includes the earlier ₹760 review order and the new ₹640 order.

13
00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:44.940
Cart actions are browser events; order_created is a trusted server event.

14
00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:48.940
The browser cannot claim order_created. Trusted server ingestion uses a separate private credential.

15
00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:54.940
The Today preset and native date pickers change the queried UTC reporting range.

16
00:01:54.940 --> 00:02:00.940
Selecting a day with no activity returns zero counts and empty lists. The complete end date is included.

17
00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:04.940
Stable event IDs support deduplication; a transaction protects local order/event consistency.

18
00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:08.940
SQLite has a single writer and synchronous queries. Browser delivery is best effort.

19
00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:12.940
Production work includes user authentication, durable outboxes, retention, monitoring, and backups.

20
00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:17.940
Install Node 24, run npm ci, and then npm run dev.

21
00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:22.940
Fourteen tests, formatting checks, the production build, and repository CI passed. See README for setup and limitations.
